From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Settings > Apps > Android apps

Android apps run in Waydroid on NickelOS (nickel-waydroid). This adds an
Android apps card to the Apps page, between Default apps and Linux apps:

- Before Android is set up: "Run Android apps" and Set up, which
  downloads Android (LineageOS from the Waydroid project, about 1 GB),
  with its progress and Cancel.
- Once set up: Android settings (Android's own Settings app, launched
  through nickel-appd as org.nickelos.AndroidSettings), how much space
  Android takes, the ARM app support switch, and Remove Android.
- ARM app support installs a translator for apps built only for ARM
  processors: Intel's Houdini on Intel CPUs, Google's NDK translation on
  AMD. NickelOS neither makes nor includes it; turning the switch on
  first shows a dialog saying so (proprietary software, under its
  owner's terms, that the user installs), and the switch stays off
  unless the user agrees. Removing Android asks first too.
- Changes are for the device's administrators: nickel-waydroidd checks,
  and the card says so to everyone else.

NickelAndroidAppsHandler talks to nickel-waydroidd (org.nickelos.Android,
system bus); the card polls its state every second while something is
under way.

Ash's UrlHandlerService, which opens the links Linux apps open, also
takes chrome://os-settings links now (shown in the Settings window, as
Ash does for any): nickel-waydroid's APK handler and Waydroid's launcher
entry send people to Settings > Apps to set Android up or turn on ARM
app support, as chrome://os-settings/apps?nickel=android, which scrolls
the card into view.

The strings are in ui_chromeos_strings.grd, which few files include.

diff --git a/ash/dbus/url_handler_service_provider.cc b/ash/dbus/url_handler_service_provider.cc
index 77c747e0b4225..81d1af74c3fbd 100644
--- a/ash/dbus/url_handler_service_provider.cc
+++ b/ash/dbus/url_handler_service_provider.cc
@@ -50,7 +50,16 @@ void UrlHandlerServiceProvider::Start(
 }
 
 bool UrlHandlerServiceProvider::UrlAllowed(const GURL& gurl) const {
-  return gurl.is_valid() && allowed_url_schemes_.contains(gurl.GetScheme());
+  if (!gurl.is_valid()) {
+    return false;
+  }
+  // NickelOS: a page of ChromeOS's Settings too, which Ash shows in the
+  // Settings window: nickel-waydroid opens Settings > Apps, where Android
+  // is set up, from its APK handler and Waydroid's launcher entry.
+  if (gurl.SchemeIs("chrome") && gurl.GetHost() == "os-settings") {
+    return true;
+  }
+  return allowed_url_schemes_.contains(gurl.GetScheme());
 }
 
 void UrlHandlerServiceProvider::OpenUrl(
